<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Problem Formulation</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the domain be <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the queries in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> , and the user query be <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{Q}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let the set of available tools be</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{avail}}=\{\mathtt{T}_{1},\ldots,\mathtt{T}_{m}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>avail</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝚃</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚃</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{avail}}=\{\mathtt{T}_{1},\ldots,\mathtt{T}_{m}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each tool <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚃</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is specified by interface metadata (name, description, parameter schema, output schema). Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙶𝚃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{GT}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ground-truth answer to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> be the max tool calling limit. A task instance denoted as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(q,\mathcal{T}_{\text{avail}},K,\mathtt{GT})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>avail</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙶𝚃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(q,\mathcal{T}_{\text{avail}},K,\mathtt{GT}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{M_{1},M_{2},\ldots,M_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{M_{1},M_{2},\ldots,M_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of LLMs and
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{A_{1},A_{2},\ldots,A_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{A_{1},A_{2},\ldots,A_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of agent frameworks.
For a given <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M,A)\in\mathcal{M}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M,A)\in\mathcal{M}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and task <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, the interaction generates a message history</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=(h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{T})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=(h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{T}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}=(r_{t}^{(M,A)},r_{t}^{\text{tool}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>tool</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}=(r_{t}^{(M,A)},r_{t}^{\text{tool}})</annotation></semantics></math> records the responses from agents and any tool invocations. The evaluation function</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:(H,\tau)\;\to\;\{0,1\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:(H,\tau)\;\to\;\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">assigns <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the user query is correctly solved under predefined success criteria, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
Correctness is determined by automated checks (e.g., verifying output content or exactly matching). Details of evaluation could be found in Sec. <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ InfoMosaic-Bench: Evaluating Multi-Source Information Seeking in Tool-Augmented Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Experiment Setup</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Models</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate a broad spectrum of current top tier LLMs, including both close-sourced and open-sourced models. Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.3.1 Models ‣ A.3 Experiment Setup ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InfoMosaic-Bench: Evaluating Multi-Source Information Seeking in Tool-Augmented Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarizes their key features such as model size, release date, openness, and access links. Through the evaluation of these latest state-of-the-art LLMs, we ensure the validity and reliability of our main conclusions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Details about evaluated LLMs.</figcaption>
